/-!
# The critical-path part of the MS93 distance-eight argument

This entry point exposes the proved critical-walk replacement tools and the
actual conjugate-generated local subgroups. It also exposes precise output
contracts for the pending local commutator and prescribed-conjugator proofs.
The final-calculation extension proves both local calculations of (4.4.5),
constructs the full natural section, and derives local centrality, b = 8 and
both edge indices. Its SourceIntegration family starts with b>4 and the exact
earlier controls and extended path, supplies the numerical fixed-factor bound,
and constructs CoreFactors.Earlier. The DistanceEight parent retains discharge
of those earlier LocalCommutator and RegularPaths inputs; the final calculation
is a completed conditional source family.

Source: Meierfrankenfeld--Stellmacher (1993), printed pp.890--895.
-/
